function tt_entry_instructions(): void { ?>
<section class="card entry-instructions">
  <h2>How Tabletime works</h2>
  <p><strong>Posts and Messages:</strong> Message remains a post type. Use <strong>Comment</strong> to reply to an existing post; Tabletime does not create a separate “reply as message” item.</p>
  <p><strong>Karma and Moksha:</strong> Karma rates posts. Moksha rates user profiles. Open a username through <strong>People</strong> to view that profile, its posts, profile picture/media, and set or update your Moksha rating.</p>
  <p><strong>Scope:</strong> the scope slider moves continuously between private, public, and global visibility. The middle/default region is public; moving toward either end blends the visibility behavior toward private or global.</p>
  <p><strong>Time delay:</strong> Tabletime displays your current posting and messaging delay on Home. Successful activity follows the configured timing rules; failed attempts can increase the active delay, and profile Moksha participates in the account delay formula.</p>
  <p><strong>Ads:</strong> Tabletime uses natural ad credits only in this build. <strong>1 ad credit = 1 counted impression.</strong> Publishing a post earns <strong>3 free ad credits</strong>. Boosting spends credits; hosting another user’s counted ad impression on your profile/home ad space earns a credit.</p>
  <p><strong>Profiles:</strong> a profile-update post can include an image. That image is used as the profile picture when no newer dedicated profile image has been uploaded. Profile pages link back to the user’s visible posts.</p>
</section>
